capstone passes its handle around as csh, a size_t, and casts it back to
struct cs_struct * in every API function, so under Fil-C every call after
cs_open trapped. Register handles in an exact pointer table: csh keeps the
pointer's address (so the API and FFI bindings are unchanged) and decoding
recovers the capability. The three (csh)&handle calls on a stack copy now
pass the real handle.

cs_option takes pointer-valued options (CS_OPT_MEM, CS_OPT_SKIPDATA_SETUP,
CS_OPT_MNEMONIC) as a size_t too; the caller's cast drops the capability
before the library sees it. Add a Fil-C-only cs_option_ptr for those and use
it in the tests.

